<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · ideology</p><h1 class="enc-title">Communism</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1793">1793 CE</a> – present</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Communism is the ideology of a classless, stateless society based on common ownership. Given its modern definition by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-marx">Marx</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-engels">Engels</a> in 1848, it took power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1917 and later ruled more than a third of the world’s population; its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/one-party-state">one-party states</a> industrialised and spread literacy, but also carried out purges, famines and repression whose death toll is still debated.</p></div>
